The copy constructor is already about as cheap as it can be. Each vector copy makes one exact-size allocation and copy-constructs the elements, and empty vectors don't allocate at all. Any real speedup has to come from elsewhere, such as avoiding `Mesg` copies at the call sites or making `Field` cheaper to copy.

This version only adds `noexcept`-free range-construction of the two vectors. The behaviour is identical:

- Same per-element copy constructors.
- Same member initialization order.
- Same exception behaviour.

Expect no measurable change in decode time.

```cpp
Mesg::Mesg(const Mesg &mesg)
    : profile(mesg.profile)
    , localNum(mesg.localNum)
    , fields(mesg.fields.begin(), mesg.fields.end())
    , devFields(mesg.devFields.begin(), mesg.devFields.end())
{
}
```